Thisbill:
I. Transfers authority over pooled risk management programs from the secretary of state to the
insurancedepartment.
II. Requirespooledriskmanagementprogramstobelicensedbytheinsurancedepartment.
III. Allows pooled risk management programs to establish a guaranty fund to protect from
financialimpairment.
IV. Requires pooled risk management programs to seek to maintain certain amounts in excess
or stop loss coverage, unless the insurance commissioner determines that a lesser amount is
appropriate.
V. Allowspooledriskmanagementprogramstoissueassessablepolicies.
